WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.735
Vision Two turns football penalty video into structured, reviewable evidence.

2
00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:08.484
This project connects computer vision with human judgement.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.593
The dataset covers thirty-nine penalties from four twenty-eighteen World Cup shoot-outs.

4
00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:20.939
Shared clip identifiers connect model observations, human labels, and final feature tables.

5
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:25.591
Pretrained YOLO eleven models extract observations.

6
00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:30.768
Optical flow compensates for camera motion, while motion-constrained beam search links ball

7
00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:31.670
detections.

8
00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:34.995
Human review resolves uncertain cases.

9
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.571
This original frame shows the selected taker and retained pose keypoints.

10
00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:45.206
In this example, the automatic and manual counts both equal four.

11
00:00:45.893 --> 00:00:49.805
A successful example does not establish accuracy across the dataset.

12
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:56.282
These four original frames run from one second before the kick to point eight seconds afterwards.

13
00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:59.460
Yellow circles mark goalkeeper positions.

14
00:01:00.147 --> 00:01:05.552
The exported movement is a low dive towards image left, with automatic quality checks accepted.

15
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:11.636
The ball sequence samples frames sixty-seven, seventy-four and seventy-six.

16
00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:16.646
Yellow circles show selected candidates; magenta crosses show ankle anchors.

17
00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:22.338
Detector confidence and quality-check acceptance do not independently verify every tracked point.

18
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:27.893
Automatic counting produced thirty-five outputs, with four failures.

19
00:01:28.578 --> 00:01:33.603
Against manually confirmed counts, mean absolute error is two point six five seven steps and

20
00:01:33.603 --> 00:01:36.653
root mean squared error is three point three seven six.

21
00:01:37.341 --> 00:01:40.658
Four predictions match exactly; twelve are within one step.

22
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:47.549
Automatic quality checks accepted eighteen goalkeeper records and twenty-six ball trajectories.

23
00:01:48.235 --> 00:01:50.423
The remaining records require review.

24
00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:55.436
These acceptance counts measure quality-control status, not detection accuracy.

25
00:01:57.017 --> 00:02:00.565
The result is an auditable dataset, with explicit uncertainty.

26
00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:05.984
Explore the methods, limitations, and all thirty-nine penalties in the Vision Two case study

27
00:02:05.984 --> 00:02:07.323
on my portfolio.
